-- title:
--   First-component chart-local membership from regularity on the ∞-side
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^2\nmid M$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$, and $M/p\neq 0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Write $F_M$ for `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, $F_{M/p}$ for the corresponding field at level $M/p$ with the image subgroup `infSubgroup p M H hpM`, and $\bar F$ for the $q$-expansion function field `JHNeronObjectAtP.Fbar p M H hpM κ`. Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of $F_M$, and $\alpha:F_{M/p}\to F_M$ an integral $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra map that is the identity on underlying Laurent series. Let `Psp` be a specialization datum, carrying a map $\mathrm{sp}$ from places of $F_{M/p}$ to places of $\bar F$ together with its $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ homomorphism and divisor, surjectivity, inertia and Frobenius compatibilities, and let `Rpd` consist of two regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to $F_M$ with residues in $\bar F$, with $R_1$ compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series and $R_2$ the $\theta$-pullback of $R_1$. Assume that on $\alpha$-images the two residues differ by the $p$-power $q$-expansion Frobenius `qExpFrobeniusModL`. Let $v$ be a place of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$ and $S\subseteq F_M$ satisfy `Rpd.IsCuspChartFstAt α hα v S`, i.e. the members of $S$ are $R_1$-integral, have residues in the valuation ring of $v$, lie in every place $W$ of $F_M$ with $\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha)=v$, the $\alpha$-images that are $R_1$-integral and integral at all places of $F_{M/p}$ specializing to $v$ become fractions $s/e$ with $s,e\in S$ and $R_1$-residue of $e$ not $0$ at $v$, there is an étale chart generator as in `ChartEtaleAt`, and every $0$-side place $W$ with $\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha)=v$ is separated by some $u\in S$ with nonvanishing residue at $v$ and $\operatorname{ord}_W u>0$. Assume further that every place $W$ of $F_M$ with $\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha)=v$ is either $\infty$-side or $0$-side. Then for $f\in R_1$ with $\operatorname{ord}_W f\ge 0$ at every $\infty$-side place $W$ with $\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha)=v$, one has $f\in$ `Rpd.chartLocalSetFst v S`: there are $g,u$ in the subring generated by $S$ with $u$ $R_1$-integral, the $R_1$-residue of $u$ not taking the value $0$ at $v$, and $fu=g$.
--
--   This is the chart-splitting step in the local analysis of $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing $M$, where the fibre has two components meeting at the supersingular points and places over a fixed fibre place $v$ are sorted into an $\infty$-side and a $0$-side; it says that integrality for the first Gauss prolongation together with regularity along the $\infty$-side forces membership in the chart-local ring attached to $v$ and the chart $S$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.cuspLocalSemicontinuityInfty_prolongationDatum_of_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.cuspLocalSemicontinuityInfty_prolongationDatum_of_residue), which transfers this membership to the cuspidal semicontinuity statement for the Deligne–Rapoport model.
